SUMMARY:Data Sharing\, Integration\, and Transition in Orthodontic Informat
 ics
LOCATION:Ortho seminar room\, School of Dental Medicine – Orthodontics\, 
 Case Western Reserve University
DESCRIPTION:An introduction to orthodontic informatics for first-year ortho
 dontic residents. Starting with computers as everyday clinical tools\, thi
 s lecture examines clinical data sharing\, repeated manual workarounds\, a
 nd the difficulty of reusing work across disconnected software. Residents 
 will consider what software integration and transitions between systems re
 quire to keep clinical data and the work built on it reusable.
